ParrotDroid is a high-pressure Android-based security lab built on Parrot OS, running inside QEMU/KVM to bring a mobile penetration-testing environment into the palm of your hand.

This project is designed for authorized cybersecurity research, ethical red teaming, and responsible wireless security testing. It is built to support those who want a portable, hardened, and tool-rich environment for learning and security assessment under proper legal authorization.

---

## Mission

ParrotDroid exists to push offensive security tooling into a mobile-first workflow:

- Run Parrot Security on Android via QEMU/KVM
- Mobilize WiFi assessment tools
- Build a portable exploitation and reconnaissance lab
- Keep a modern security toolkit accessible on the go
- Provide a toolchain for ethical testing and research

---

## Core Features

- Parrot OS guest environment inside Android
- KVM-backed virtualization for mobile deployment
- WiFi auditing and reconnaissance support via usb passthrough
- Portable offensive security lab
- Full Parrot Security ecosystem integration
- Customizable development and testing workflow
- Security-focused toolkit for legal auditing and research

